    primaryQuestion: "How does IVF work step by step?",
    directAnswer: "In vitro fertilisation means eggs and sperm meet outside the body. The UK Human Fertilisation and Embryology Authority (HFEA) describes a typical cycle as ovarian stimulation with monitoring, egg collection, mixing eggs with sperm in a laboratory, embryo development for about two to six days, then embryo transfer—with remaining suitable embryos often frozen. HFEA notes one cycle commonly takes about three to six weeks depending on the protocol. No stage guarantees the next, and pathways differ by history and clinic plan.",
