        heading: "When to seek urgent care while using or considering HRT",
        paragraphs: [
          "Seek emergency care for symptoms of a possible clot or stroke—sudden chest pain, coughing blood, severe calf swelling and pain, sudden weakness, speech difficulty or collapse—or for heavy bleeding with fainting. Any bleeding after confirmed menopause still needs prompt assessment even if you are not on HRT.",
          "Book a non-urgent review if side effects persist, bleeding on HRT stays irregular beyond the early adjustment window your clinician described, or symptoms are uncontrolled. Alternatives and follow-up timing belong in that visit, not in self-adjustment of doses."
        ]
